WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:05.297
P4.4 · Exporting the forecast to a TMS or a file

2
00:00:06.447 --> 00:00:13.871
K-φ turns the forecast into liquidity entries: a plan, a company, a budget code, an amount, a due date.

3
00:00:13.921 --> 00:00:17.561
That is what a treasury system such as Kyriba imports.

4
00:00:18.711 --> 00:00:27.225
On the K-φ Forecast, Export to TMS: tick the lines to send and give each its budget code, the one your TMS knows.

5
00:00:27.275 --> 00:00:32.651
Generate Entries makes one entry per line and month. Months at zero are left out.

6
00:00:33.801 --> 00:00:41.767
A line goes rolled up, one entry a month, or in detail: its chevron sends one entry per account family, same totals.

7
00:00:41.817 --> 00:00:46.759
The Liquidity Plan field is the identifier your TMS reads from the file.

8
00:00:47.909 --> 00:00:52.645
The Forecast List is the outbox, with the scenarios you send from Simulate.

9
00:00:52.695 --> 00:00:57.946
Download gives the TMS file. Format and Value Mapping fit it to your template.

10
00:00:57.996 --> 00:01:00.513
K Upload sends it straight to Kyriba.

11
00:01:01.663 --> 00:01:07.077
Without a budget, the run rate shows on screen and is left out of every treasury export.

12
00:01:09.963 --> 00:01:13.210
Next: P5.1  Building a scenario

